### Unit Test for Hypergeometric Distribution - Sample Size Larger Than Population Size

We need to ensure that when the sample size (k) is larger than the population size (N), we throw a `NumberIsTooLargeException` as described in the code.

Here's our test class:

```java
public class HypergeometricDistributionTest {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Set up expectations
        org.junit.Assert.that(NumberIsTooLargeException.class).isThrowing(42, "This test should be thrown for sample size too large than population size.");

        // Create the distribution object (parameters don't matter in this case)
        DoubleDistribution hypergeometricDist = HypergeometricDistributionImpl(
            100, // population size N
            50   // number of success states in population
        );

        // Test if calculation is thrown for too large sample size
        try {
            double mean = hypergeometricDist.getNumericalMean();
            // Expect that NumberIsTooLargeException was thrown
            NumberIsTooLargeException expectException(hypergeometricDist);

            // Verify that the method doesn't return incorrect results
            assertEquals(0.5, mean, 2);
        } catch (NumberIsTooLargeException e) {
            expectException(e, "The sample size cannot exceed the population size.");
        }
    }


    private double getNumericalMean() {
        // In case of too large sample size, exception is thrown before this can be calculated.
        return getNumSamples() * ((getNumberOfSuccesses() / (double) getPopulationSize()) - (1 / (double) getPopulationSize()));
    }
}
